  {
   "id": 1,
   "type": "text",
   "title": "",
   "gridPos": {
    "x": 0,
    "y": 0,
    "w": 13,
    "h": 4
   },
   "options": {
    "mode": "markdown",
    "content": "## IEC 61162-450 ping-pong test  \n**GE1 sends** the 450 sample mix on every multicast group, **GE9 receives and echoes** each datagram back on the same group, GE1 receives the reply, and this repeats for the whole run. The **ONF dump** (chart data, unicast port 20100) goes both ways and carries the bulk of the load, because one sensor may only send 13 sentences/s.  \n**message** = one 450 sample (sentence / binary block / syslog line) &nbsp; **packet** = any UDP datagram (mix + ONF dump) &nbsp; **data** = payload bytes. Loss comes from in-band sequence numbers. Port utilisation comes from the switch (SNMP, 5 s)."
   }
  },
